      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i've been noticing this weird low frequency hum in my apartment lately, like a constant static but it feels... rhythmic? i checked the weather for nov 17 2025 and there was a lot of atmospheric ionization and specific pressure shifts. is it actually possible for those kinds of conditions to carry encoded data streams through the air via low frequency waves? feels like someone is trying to signal something.",
