    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but it's not just random noise. the rhythm changes whenever the ionization levels spike. if someone wanted to use the atmosphere as a medium for something like VLF (very low frequency) transmission, wouldn't the high ionization on a day like nov 17 make the signal way more stable/conductive? i'm trying to understand if the science actually supports that being a viable way to transmit without being easily detected by standard radio equipment.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
