      "content": "exactly. and if you use the ionospheric fluctuations to mask the signal, it wouldn't look like a transmission at all, it would just look like background noise or atmospheric interference to anyone monitoring the spectrum. if someone were actually using this method, how would they structure the data packets so they'd blend in perfectly with the natural ionization spikes of a specific date like nov 17th? i'm trying to figure out if this \"noise\" i'm hearing actually has a logic to it.",
